<title>USA: Oakley sees impact from order cancellations.</title>
<headline>Oakley sees impact from order cancellations.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oakley Inc said while it was pleased with its overall growth for all of 1996, it was &quot;disappointed&quot; with its fourth quarter results.</p>
<p>In large part, the quarter's results reflected declining sales and order cancellations by its largest retailer, Sunglass Hut, and poor holiday business for its retail products, said Mike Parnell, Oakley's chief executive officer.</p>
<p>He made the comment as the designer eyeglass maker reported fourth quarter net sales of $39.3 million, down from $43.0 million for the prior year.</p>
</text>
